1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,970
SkinCeuticals C E Ferulic costs $185.

2
00:00:03,990 --> 00:00:08,400
Timeless sells a $28 serum with the same first three ingredients.

3
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:12,360
If you use vitamin C, or you've been eyeing that bottle, this is for you.

4
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:21,810
The original patent expired in 2025, so this is The Formula Folio, reading both labels to see what $157 more actually buys.

5
00:00:21,830 --> 00:00:25,060
On the left, SkinCeuticals C E Ferulic.

6
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:28,310
It's built on research from a Duke dermatology lab.

7
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:34,970
That work found vitamin C, vitamin E and ferulic acid together gave about eight times the skin's natural protection.

8
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:38,670
On the right, Timeless 20% Vitamin C plus E and Ferulic Acid.

9
00:00:38,690 --> 00:00:42,210
It's one of the most-reviewed serums sold as an alternative.

10
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:45,100
First, what the patent actually protected.

11
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:47,200
It didn't cover vitamin C itself.

12
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:55,300
It covered a specific combination: 15% pure vitamin C, 1% vitamin E and 0.5% ferulic acid, at a specific low pH.

13
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:57,160
That protection ended in March 2025.

14
00:00:57,180 --> 00:01:01,430
Since then, other brands can use the same three percentages, and some already do.

15
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:05,710
Drunk Elephant's C-Firma is one example.

16
00:01:05,730 --> 00:01:12,260
But matching the numbers on a label doesn't prove a bottle performs the same.

17
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:15,100
Stability, pH and packaging matter too, and most of that isn't printed.

18
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:16,750
So let's read what is.

19
00:01:16,770 --> 00:01:19,840
Same first three ingredients, in the same order.

20
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:22,460
Water.

21
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:24,620
Ethoxydiglycol, a solvent that helps vitamin C get into skin.

22
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:28,700
Then ascorbic acid, the pure form of vitamin C.

23
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:30,470
SkinCeuticals says 15%.

24
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:32,760
Timeless says 20%.

25
00:01:32,780 --> 00:01:36,400
More isn't automatically better.

26
00:01:36,420 --> 00:01:41,320
Pure vitamin C works at a very low pH, and higher strengths sting more.

27
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:43,860
Fifteen percent is already a strong dose.

28
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:48,620
Eight of Timeless's eleven ingredients also appear in SkinCeuticals.

29
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,350
Vitamin E, ferulic acid, panthenol, hyaluronic acid.

30
00:01:52,370 --> 00:01:54,540
The core idea is the same.

31
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:59,150
Here's a trick you can use on any label.

32
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:01,060
Phenoxyethanol, a preservative, is capped at 1%.

33
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:04,400
So everything listed after it is 1% or less.

34
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:09,600
That includes the two new ingredients SkinCeuticals added: 0.3% carnosine, and Endophytol, a dandelion root extract.

35
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:12,610
They say Endophytol is 1%.

36
00:02:12,630 --> 00:02:17,930
On the label it appears as dandelion root extract, followed by maltodextrin, a common carrier powder.

37
00:02:17,950 --> 00:02:23,420
The new formula comes with a new claim: it visibly reverses ten years of aging signs.

38
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:26,580
What's disclosed is a twelve-week study.

39
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,780
Not how many people.

40
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,100
Not how it was measured.

41
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:33,810
'Visibly' means it was judged by eye, not by a lab instrument.

42
00:02:33,830 --> 00:02:36,690
That doesn't make it false.

43
00:02:36,710 --> 00:02:38,770
It means we can't check it.

44
00:02:38,790 --> 00:02:44,830
Timeless publishes one small study: 21 people over 28 days, run by a third party, also judged by appearance.

45
00:02:44,850 --> 00:02:49,790
It doesn't print its vitamin E and ferulic acid percentages.

46
00:02:49,810 --> 00:02:51,170
SkinCeuticals does: 1 and 0.5.

47
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:57,170
At four to five drops a morning, a bottle lasts roughly four months.

48
00:02:57,190 --> 00:02:59,130
That's about $46 a month against about $7.

49
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:03,020
And vitamin C oxidizes once it's open.

50
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:06,700
SkinCeuticals itself says to use a bottle within three to six months.

51
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:10,660
A cheaper bottle you finish fresh can beat an expensive one you stretch.

52
00:03:10,680 --> 00:03:15,720
Before the verdict, here's how to check any vitamin C serum yourself, in four steps.

53
00:03:15,740 --> 00:03:18,260
One, the form.

54
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:23,800
Look for ascorbic acid, or L-ascorbic acid, near the top of the list.

55
00:03:23,820 --> 00:03:26,300
That's the pure form both of these use.

56
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:33,900
Derivatives, like sodium ascorbyl phosphate or ascorbyl glucoside, are gentler, but they have less research behind them for the same results.

57
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:34,720
Two, the strength.

58
00:03:34,740 --> 00:03:40,930
Research on pure vitamin C found skin absorbs it best up to about 20%.

59
00:03:40,950 --> 00:03:43,350
Past that, you mostly add sting.

60
00:03:43,370 --> 00:03:44,900
Three, the backup.

61
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:49,160
Vitamin E and ferulic acid help keep vitamin C stable and working.

62
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:49,860
Four, the bottle.

63
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:55,620
Dark or opaque glass, and a size you'll finish within the brand's window after opening.

64
00:03:55,640 --> 00:03:58,360
Notice what's not on that list: the price.

65
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:00,050
So, the verdict.

66
00:04:00,070 --> 00:04:07,940
Pay for SkinCeuticals if you want the exact ratio behind twenty years of published research, or your dermatologist pairs it with procedures.

67
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:13,680
If you want the core trio in a similar base for a sixth of the price, Timeless gets you close.

68
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:15,500
Close, not identical.

69
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,140
A note for deeper skin.

70
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:19,550
Vitamin C can help fade dark marks.

71
00:04:19,570 --> 00:04:25,320
But irritation from strong, low-pH serums can leave new ones on deeper skin.

72
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:27,850
Patch test, and start every other morning.

73
00:04:27,870 --> 00:04:30,210
Own a luxury serum we haven't tested?

74
00:04:30,230 --> 00:04:33,020
Film a 10-second swipe for the Folio Bench.

75
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,980
Instructions are in the description.

76
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,920
This is The Formula Folio.

77
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:40,380
We read the formula, so you don't overpay.
